First, let's find an expression for $\dfrac{d}{dx}[3g(x)-8h(x)+4]$ in terms of $g'$ and $h'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}[3g(x)-8h(x)+4]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[3g(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}[8h(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}(4)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=3g'(x)-8h'(x)+0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $\dfrac{d}{dx}[3g(x)-8h(x)+4]=3g'(x)-8h'(x)$.
